{"name":"Döner Kebab","hex":"#bb7766","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"döner kebab","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of doner kebab."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/d%C3%B6ner_kebab"}],"entries":[{"title":"Doner kebab","blocks":[{"text":"Doner kebab or döner kebab is a Turkish dish made of meat cooked on a vertical rotisserie. Seasoned meat stacked in the shape of an inverted cone is turned slowly on the rotisserie, next to a vertical cooking element. The operator uses a knife to slice thin shavings from the outer layer of the meat as it cooks. The vertical rotisserie was invented in the 19th-century Ottoman Empire, and dishes such as the Arab shawarma, Greek gyros, Greek-Canadian donair, and Mexican al pastor are derived from the rotisserie technique of this dish."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ad/D%C3%B6ner_kebab_slicing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doner_kebab","wikidata":"Q20734"},{"title":"Kebab","blocks":[{"text":"Kebab, kebap, kabob, kebob, or kabab (Kashmiri) is a variety of roasted meat dishes that originated in the Middle East."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Lula_kebab_2.jpg/330px-Lula_kebab_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kebab","wikidata":"Q179010"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/D%C3%B6nerci%2C_1855.jpg/500px-D%C3%B6nerci%2C_1855.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/D%C3%B6nerci%2C_1855.jpg/500px-D%C3%B6nerci%2C_1855.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The earliest known photo of döner, by James Robertson, 1855, Ottoman Empire","link":"https://en.wik